Description: Auto-enable controllers that have never been configured
 DecksmithOS runs Mixxx as an appliance without mouse or keyboard, so a
 plugged-in controller has to work without visiting the preferences.
 On start-up, a controller with no "[Controller]" entry and no configured
 mapping is enabled when exactly one installed mapping matches it:
 HID/bulk devices by the product IDs declared in the mappings (the existing
 Controller::matchMapping), MIDI devices by name (every word of the device
 name, minus the "MIDI n" port suffix, must appear in the mapping name or
 file name; fewest additional words wins; ties and generic names such as
 "USB MIDI" are rejected). Explicit user choices stored in the config,
 including a disabled controller, always take precedence.
Author: DecksmithOS
Forwarded: no
